---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="Moving from Kenya to Australia: The Complete Guide | AfriMigrate"
  description="A complete, free guide to moving from Kenya to Australia — skills assessment, the points test, visa subclasses, and what to expect."
>
  <div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/blog">Blog</a> / Kenya to Australia</div>
  <div class="eyebrow">Guide · Kenya → Australia</div>
  <h1>Moving from Kenya to Australia: The Complete Guide</h1>
  <p class="lead" style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
    Kenyan professionals in engineering, ICT, healthcare and accounting have a genuine no-job-offer route into Australia through the points-tested skilled migration program. Here's how it works.
  </p>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="eyebrow">Step 1</div>
    <h2>Get your skills assessed</h2>
    <p class="lead" style="max-width: 700px;">
      This is the mandatory first step, and it's where most delays happen. Find your occupation's assessing body and start gathering reference letters and transcripts as early as possible — some assessments take several months.
    </p>
    <a href="/australia/skills-assessment" class="btn-primary" style="margin-top: 0.5rem;">Find my assessing body →</a>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="eyebrow">Step 2</div>
    <h2>Score yourself against the points test</h2>
    <p class="lead" style="max-width: 700px;">
      Age and English ability carry the most weight, and a state or territory nomination can add points and open up the subclass 190 or 491 visas even if your subclass 189 score is a little short.
    </p>
    <a href="/australia/points-calculator" class="btn-primary" style="margin-top: 0.5rem;">Calculate my points →</a>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="eyebrow">Step 3</div>
    <h2>Understand the invitation system</h2>
    <p class="lead" style="max-width: 700px;">
      After submitting an Expression of Interest, you wait to be invited in a points-ranked round. Higher scores get invited sooner — this is why maximising your English test result before submitting often pays off more than waiting.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="manifesto">
      <h2>No consultant. <em>No fortune spent.</em></h2>
      <p>Everything above is public information — AfriMigrate just puts it in one place, in plain English, for free.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
